adjudication.rationale:
In the newly added API route `apps/web/pages/api/webhook/app-credential.ts`, the webhook authentication check directly compares the provided header to `process.env.CALCOM_WEBHOOK_SECRET` using `!==`:

```ts
if (
  req.headers[process.env.CALCOM_WEBHOOK_HEADER_NAME || "calcom-webhook-secret"] !==
  process.env.CALCOM_WEBHOOK_SECRET
) {
  return res.status(403).json({ message: "Invalid webhook secret" });
}
```

A plain string/byte comparison with `!==` is not constant-time and can be vulnerable to timing side-channels when used for secret validation. Using `crypto.timingSafeEqual` (with proper Buffer conversion and length check) is the standard mitigation. This is a real, diff-introduced security concern in the webhook secret verification logic.
